{"name":"Ghost","hex":"#c0bfc7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ghost","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A disembodied soul; a soul or spirit of a deceased person; a spirit appearing after death.","A spirit; a human soul."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["In the form be ghost: not present or involved; absent, gone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ghost"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ghost","blocks":[{"text":"In folklore, a ghost is the soul or spirit of a dead person or non-human animal that is believed by some people to be able to appear to the living. In ghostlore, descriptions of ghosts vary widely, from an invisible presence to translucent or barely visible wispy shapes to realistic, lifelike forms, whether they resemble humans or animals. The deliberate attempt to contact the spirit of a deceased person is known as necromancy, or in spiritism as a séance. Other terms associated with it are apparition, haunt, haint, phantom, poltergeist, shade, specter, spirit, spook, wraith, demon, and ghoul."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/02/Hammersmith_Ghost.PNG/330px-Hammersmith_Ghost.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost","wikidata":"Q45529"},{"title":"Ghost (Swedish band)","blocks":[{"text":"Ghost is a Swedish rock band formed in Linköping, in 2006. The band released their debut album, Opus Eponymous, in 2010, which earned them international recognition. This was followed by Infestissumam in 2013 and in 2015 by Meliora, which reached number one in Sweden and number eight in the US. This was followed by the albums Prequelle in 2018 and Impera in 2022. The band's sixth studio album, Skeletá, was released in 2025; it subsequently became their first number one on the US Billboard 200 chart."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/2023_Sweden_Rock_-_4309_%2853048871172%29.jpg/330px-2023_Sweden_Rock_-_4309_%2853048871172%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_(Swedish_band)","wikidata":"Q1355578"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/NAMA_Herm%C3%A8s_%26_Myrrhin%C3%A8.jpg/500px-NAMA_Herm%C3%A8s_%26_Myrrhin%C3%A8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/NAMA_Herm%C3%A8s_%26_Myrrhin%C3%A8.jpg/500px-NAMA_Herm%C3%A8s_%26_Myrrhin%C3%A8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Relief from a carved funerary lekythos at Athens showing Hermes as psychopomp conducting the soul of the deceased, Myrrhine into Hades (c. 430–420 BC)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANAMA_Herm%C3%A8s_%26_Myrrhin%C3%A8.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Suushi_Yurei.jpg/250px-Suushi_Yurei.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a0/Suushi_Yurei.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Suushi_Yurei.jpg/250px-Suushi_Yurei.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Yūrei (Japanese ghost) from the Hyakkai Zukan, c. 1737","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASuushi_Yurei.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Union_Graveyard_III.jpg/500px-Union_Graveyard_III.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Union_Graveyard_III.jpg/1280px-Union_Graveyard_III.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Union_Graveyard_III.jpg/500px